{"id":"mahabharata-3-190","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":190,"title":"नवत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 190 · King Parikshit and the frog princess","summary":{"en":"Markandeya tells, partly in prose, of King Parikshit of Ayodhya, who married a frog king's daughter on condition that she never see water, and of their son Shala, who stole the sage Vamadeva's horses and was punished; Vamadeva's power and the queen's plea show the might of Brahmins.","kn":"ನೀರನ್ನು ಎಂದೂ ಕಾಣಬಾರದೆಂಬ ಷರತ್ತಿನೊಂದಿಗೆ ಕಪ್ಪೆರಾಜನ ಮಗಳನ್ನು ಮದುವೆಯಾದ ಅಯೋಧ್ಯೆಯ ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿತರಾಜನನ್ನೂ, ವಾಮದೇವ ಋಷಿಯ ಕುದುರೆಗಳನ್ನು ಕದ್ದು ಶಿಕ್ಷೆಗೊಳಗಾದ ಅವರ ಮಗ ಶಲನನ್ನೂ ಕುರಿತು ಮಾರ್ಕಂಡೇಯರು ಭಾಗಶಃ ಗದ್ಯದಲ್ಲಿ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾರೆ; ವಾಮದೇವನ ಶಕ್ತಿ ಮತ್ತು ರಾಣಿಯ ಬೇಡಿಕೆ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣರ ಮಹಿಮೆಯನ್ನು ತೋರುತ್ತವೆ.","hi":"मार्कण्डेय कुछ गद्य में अयोध्या के राजा परीक्षित की कथा सुनाते हैं, जिन्होंने मेंढक-राज की पुत्री से इस शर्त पर विवाह किया कि वह कभी जल न देखे, और उनके पुत्र शल की, जिसने ऋषि वामदेव के घोड़े चुराए और दण्ड पाया; वामदेव की शक्ति और रानी की विनती ब्राह्मणों की महिमा दिखाती है।","te":"నీటిని ఎన్నడూ చూడకూడదనే షరతుతో కప్పరాజు కుమార్తెను వివాహమాడిన అయోధ్యరాజు పరీక్షిత్తు గురించి, వామదేవ ఋషి గుర్రాలను దొంగిలించి శిక్ష పొందిన వారి కుమారుడు శలుని గురించి మార్కండేయుడు కొంత గద్యంలో చెబుతాడు; వామదేవుని శక్తి, రాణి వేడుకోలు బ్రాహ్మణుల మహిమను చూపుతాయి.","ta":"நீரை ஒருபோதும் பார்க்கக் கூடாது என்ற நிபந்தனையுடன் தவளை அரசனின் மகளை மணந்த அயோத்தி மன்னன் பரீக்ஷித்தையும், வாமதேவ முனிவரின் குதிரைகளைத் திருடித் தண்டனை பெற்ற அவர்கள் மகன் ஶலனையும் பற்றி மார்க்கண்டேயர் பகுதியாக உரைநடையில் சொல்கிறார்; வாமதேவரின் ஆற்றலும் அரசியின் வேண்டுதலும் அந்தணர்களின் பெருமையைக் காட்டுகின்றன.","ml":"മാർക്കണ്ഡേയൻ ഭാഗികമായി ഗദ്യരൂപത്തിൽ പറയുന്ന കഥ: അയോധ്യയിലെ പരീക്ഷിത്ത് രാജാവ് ഒരു തവളരാജാവിന്റെ മകളെ വിവാഹം ചെയ്തു; ഒരിക്കലും വെള്ളം കാണരുതെന്നായിരുന്നു വ്യവസ്ഥ. അവരുടെ പുത്രനായ ശാലൻ വാമദേവമുനിയുടെ കുതിരകളെ മോഷ്ടിച്ച് ശിക്ഷിക്കപ്പെടുന്നു; വാമദേവന്റെ ശക്തിയും രാജ്ഞിയുടെ അപേക്ഷയും ബ്രാഹ്മണരുടെ മഹത്വം കാണിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.190; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"मार्कण्डेयसमास्यापर्व","titleEn":"Markandeyasamasya Parva (Session with Markandeya)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"भूय एव ब्राह्मणमहाभाग्यं वक्तुमर्हसीत्यब्रवीत्पाण्डवेयो मार्कण्डेयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandava said to Markandeya, \"You should tell us more of the greatness of brahmins.\""}},{"n":2,"text":"अथाचष्ट मार्कण्डेयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Markandeya told this."}},{"n":3,"text":"अयोध्यायामिक्ष्वाकुकुलोत्पन्नः पार्थिवः परिक्षिन्नाम मृगयामगमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In Ayodhya there was a king of the Ikshvaku line named Parikshit, who went out hunting."}},{"n":4,"text":"तमेकाश्वेन मृगमनुसरन्तं मृगो दूरमपाहरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he chased a deer alone on his horse, the deer drew him far away."}},{"n":5,"text":"अथाध्वनि जातश्रमः क्षुत्तृष्णाभिभूतश्च कस्मिंश्चिदुद्देशे नीलं वनषण्डमपश्यत् ।\nतच्च विवेश ॥","meaning":{"en":"On the way, tired and overcome by hunger and thirst, he saw a dark-green grove in one place and entered it."}},{"n":6,"text":"ततस्तस्य वनषण्डस्य मध्येऽतीव रमणीयं सरो दृष्ट्वा साश्व एव व्यगाहत ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the middle of that grove he saw an exceedingly lovely lake, and he plunged in with his horse."}},{"n":7,"text":"अथाश्वस्तः स बिसमृणालमश्वस्याग्रे निक्षिप्य पुष्करिणीतीरे समाविशत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Refreshed, he set lotus stalks before the horse and sat down on the lakeshore."}},{"n":8,"text":"ततः शयानो मधुरं गीतशब्दमशृणोत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he lay there he heard a sweet sound of singing."}},{"n":9,"text":"स श्रुत्वाचिन्तयत् ।\nनेह मनुष्यगतिं पश्यामि ।\nकस्य खल्वयं गीतशब्द इति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing it he thought, \"I see no human path here. Whose song can this be?\""}},{"n":10,"text":"अथापश्यत्कन्यां परमरूपदर्शनीयां पुष्पाण्यवचिन्वतीं गायन्तीं च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he saw a girl of supreme beauty, gathering flowers and singing."}},{"n":11,"text":"अथ सा राज्ञः समीपे पर्यक्रामत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"She walked up near the king."}},{"n":12,"text":"तामब्रवीद्राजा ।\nकस्यासि सुभगे त्वमिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king said to her, \"Fortunate one, whose daughter are you?\""}},{"n":13,"text":"सा प्रत्युवाच ।\nकन्यास्मीति ॥","meaning":{"en":"She replied, \"I am a maiden.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"तां राजोवाच ।\nअर्थी त्वयाहमिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king said to her, \"I want you.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"अथोवाच कन्या ।\nसमयेनाहं शक्या त्वया लब्धुम् ।\nनान्यथेति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The girl then said, \"You can have me only on a condition, not otherwise.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"तां राजा समयमपृच्छत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king asked her the condition."}},{"n":17,"text":"ततः कन्येदमुवाच ।\nउदकं मे न दर्शयितव्यमिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The girl then said, \"You must never show me water.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"स राजा बाढमित्युक्त्वा तां समागम्य तया सहास्ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king said, \"So be it,\" and joined her and stayed with her."}},{"n":19,"text":"तत्रैवासीने राजनि सेनान्वगच्छत् ।\nपदेनानुपदं दृष्ट्वा राजानं परिवार्यातिष्ठत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While the king sat there, his army followed his tracks, footprint by footprint, saw him and stood around him."}},{"n":20,"text":"पर्याश्वस्तश्च राजा तयैव सह शिबिकया प्रायादविघाटितया ।\nस्वनगरमनुप्राप्य रहसि तया सह रमन्नास्ते ।\nनान्यत्किंचनापश्यत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Comforted, the king set out with her in a closed palanquin; reaching his city, he stayed in private enjoying her and saw nothing else."}},{"n":21,"text":"अथ प्रधानामात्यस्तस्याभ्याशचराः स्त्रियोऽपृच्छत् ।\nकिमत्र प्रयोजनं वर्तत इति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the chief minister asked the women who attended near him, \"What is going on here?\""}},{"n":22,"text":"अथाब्रुवंस्ताः स्त्रियः ।\nअपूर्वमिव पश्याम उदकं नात्र नीयतेति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The women said, \"We see something strange: no water is brought here.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"अथामात्योऽनुदकं वनं कारयित्वोदारवृक्षं बहुमूलपुष्पफलं रहस्युपगम्य राजानमब्रवीत् ।\nवनमिदमुदारमनुदकम् ।\nसाध्वत्र रम्यतामिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The minister had a waterless garden made with fine trees full of roots, flowers and fruit, and approached the king in private. He said, \"This is a fine garden without water; take your pleasure here.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"स तस्य वचनात्तयैव सह देव्या तद्वनं प्राविशत् ।\nस कदाचित्तस्मिन्वने रम्ये तयैव सह व्यवहरत् ।\nअथ क्षुत्तृष्णार्दितः श्रान्तोऽतिमात्रमतिमुक्तागारमपश्यत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"At his word the king entered that garden with his queen. Once, while he was enjoying himself with her in that lovely garden, hungry, thirsty and tired, he saw a very beautiful pavilion of pearl."}},{"n":25,"text":"तत्प्रविश्य राजा सह प्रियया सुधातलसुकृतां विमलसलिलपूर्णां वापीमपश्यत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Entering it with his beloved, the king saw a pool filled with clear water, with a floor beautifully made of plaster."}},{"n":26,"text":"दृष्ट्वैव च तां तस्या एव तीरे सहैव तया देव्या व्यतिष्ठत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing it, he stood on its bank with the queen."}},{"n":27,"text":"अथ तां देवीं स राजाब्रवीत् ।\nसाध्ववतर वापीसलिलमिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the king said to her, \"Go down, fine lady, into the water of the pool.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"सा तद्वचः श्रुत्वावतीर्य वापीं न्यमज्जत् ।\nन पुनरुदमज्जत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, she went down into the pool and dived; she did not come up again."}},{"n":29,"text":"तां मृगयमाणो राजा नापश्यत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king searched for her and could not find her."}},{"n":30,"text":"वापीमपि निःस्राव्य मण्डूकं श्वभ्रमुखे दृष्ट्वा क्रुद्ध आज्ञापयामास ।\nसर्वमण्डूकवधः क्रियतामिति ।\nयो मयार्थी स मृतकैर्मण्डूकैरुपायनैर्मामुपतिष्ठेदिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Draining the pool, he saw a frog at the mouth of a hole and, in anger, ordered, \"Let all frogs be killed! Whoever wants to please me should present dead frogs to me as gifts.\""}},{"n":31,"text":"अथ मण्डूकवधे घोरे क्रियमाणे दिक्षु सर्वासु मण्डूकान्भयमाविशत् ।\nते भीता मण्डूकराज्ञे यथावृत्तं न्यवेदयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the dreadful killing of frogs went on, fear entered the frogs in every direction; frightened, they told their king what had happened."}},{"n":32,"text":"ततो मण्डूकराट्तापसवेषधारी राजानमभ्यगच्छत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the frog king, disguised as an ascetic, came to the king."}},{"n":33,"text":"उपेत्य चैनमुवाच ।\nमा राजन्क्रोधवशं गमः ।\nप्रसादं कुरु ।\nनार्हसि मण्डूकानामनपराधिनां वधं कर्तुमिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Coming up, he said, \"King, do not fall under the sway of anger. Be gracious; you should not kill innocent frogs.\""}},{"n":34,"text":"श्लोकौ चात्र भवतः ।\nमा मण्डूकाञ्जिघांस त्वं कोपं संधारयाच्युत ।\nप्रक्षीयते धनोद्रेको जनानामविजानताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Two verses are given here: \"Do not seek to kill frogs, unfallen one; hold your anger back. The wealth of those who act without knowing wastes away."}},{"n":35,"text":"प्रतिजानीहि नैतांस्त्वं प्राप्य क्रोधं विमोक्ष्यसे ।\nअलं कृत्वा तवाधर्मं मण्डूकैः किं हतैर्हि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Promise me this: you will not be freed from anger by gaining these frogs. Enough of your wrong-doing; what use are dead frogs to you?\""}},{"n":36,"text":"तमेवंवादिनमिष्टजनशोकपरीतात्मा राजा प्रोवाच ।\nन हि क्षम्यते तन्मया ।\nहनिष्याम्येतान् ।\nएतैर्दुरात्मभिः प्रिया मे भक्षिता ।\nसर्वथैव मे वध्या मण्डूकाः ।\nनार्हसि विद्वन्मामुपरोद्धुमिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"To him as he spoke so, the king, his mind seized with grief for his beloved, said, \"I cannot forgive it. I will kill them. These wretches ate my dear one; the frogs must be killed in every case. Learned man, you should not hold me back.\""}},{"n":37,"text":"स तद्वाक्यमुपलभ्य व्यथितेन्द्रियमनाः प्रोवाच ।\nप्रसीद राजन् ।\nअहमायुर्नाम मण्डूकराजः ।\nमम सा दुहिता सुशोभना नाम ।\nतस्या दौःशील्यमेतत् ।\nबहवो हि राजानस्तया विप्रलब्धपूर्वा इति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, his senses and mind shaken, he said, \"Be gracious, king. I am the frog king, named Ayu. That is my daughter, called Sushobhana. This is her bad habit: many kings have been cheated by her before.\""}},{"n":38,"text":"तमब्रवीद्राजा ।\nतयास्म्यर्थी ।\nसा मे दीयतामिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king said to him, \"I want her; let her be given to me.\""}},{"n":39,"text":"अथैनां राज्ञे पितादात् ।\nअब्रवीच्चैनाम् ।\nएनं राजानं शुश्रूषस्वेति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Her father then gave her to the king and said to her, \"Serve this king.\""}},{"n":40,"text":"स उवाच दुहितरम् ।\nयस्मात्त्वया राजानो विप्रलब्धास्तस्मादब्रह्मण्यानि तवापत्यानि भविष्यन्त्यनृतकत्वात्तवेति ॥","meaning":{"en":"He said to his daughter, \"Because you have cheated kings, your children will be disrespectful to brahmins, because of your falsehood.\""}},{"n":41,"text":"स च राजा तामुपलभ्य तस्यां सुरतगुणनिबद्धहृदयो लोकत्रयैश्वर्यमिवोपलभ्य हर्षबाष्पकलया वाचा प्रणिपत्याभिपूज्य मण्डूकराजानमब्रवीत् ।\nअनुगृहीतोऽस्मीति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king, having got her back, his heart bound by the pleasures of love for her, felt as if he had gained lordship of the three worlds; with joyful tears in his voice he bowed to the frog king and honoured him, saying, \"I am favoured.\""}},{"n":42,"text":"स च मण्डूकराजो जामातरमनुज्ञाप्य यथागतमगच्छत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The frog king took leave of his son-in-law and went away as he had come."}},{"n":43,"text":"अथ कस्यचित्कालस्य तस्यां कुमारास्त्रयस्तस्य राज्ञः संबभूवुः शलो दलो बलश्चेति ।\nततस्तेषां ज्येष्ठं शलं समये पिता राज्येऽभिषिच्य तपसि धृतात्मा वनं जगाम ॥","meaning":{"en":"After some time three sons were born to the king by her: Shala, Dala and Bala. The father, steadfast, consecrated the eldest, Shala, as king at the proper time and went to the forest for austerities."}},{"n":44,"text":"अथ कदाचिच्छलो मृगयामचरत् ।\nमृगं चासाद्य रथेनान्वधावत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then one day Shala went hunting; coming upon a deer, he chased it in his chariot."}},{"n":45,"text":"सूतं चोवाच ।\nशीघ्रं मां वहस्वेति ॥","meaning":{"en":"He said to the charioteer, \"Drive me fast.\""}},{"n":46,"text":"स तथोक्तः सूतो राजानमब्रवीत् ।\nमा क्रियतामनुबन्धः ।\nनैष शक्यस्त्वया मृगो ग्रहीतुं यद्यपि ते रथे युक्तौ वाम्यौ स्यातामिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Told so, the charioteer said to the king, \"Give up the pursuit. You cannot catch that deer, even if your chariot were yoked with the two horses of Vamadeva.\""}},{"n":47,"text":"ततोऽब्रवीद्राजा सूतम् ।\nआचक्ष्व मे वाम्यौ ।\nहन्मि वा त्वामिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king then said to the charioteer, \"Tell me about Vamadeva's horses, or I will kill you.\""}},{"n":48,"text":"स एवमुक्तो राजभयभीतो वामदेवशापभीतश्च सन्नाचख्यौ राज्ञे ।\nवामदेवस्याश्वौ वाम्यौ मनोजवाविति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Spoken to so, afraid of the king and afraid of Vamadeva's curse, he told the king that Vamadeva's two horses were mind-swift."}},{"n":49,"text":"अथैनमेवं ब्रुवाणमब्रवीद्राजा ।\nवामदेवाश्रमं याहीति ॥","meaning":{"en":"When he had so spoken, the king said, \"Go to Vamadeva's hermitage.\""}},{"n":50,"text":"स गत्वा वामदेवाश्रमं तमृषिमब्रवीत् ।\nभगवन्मृगो मया विद्धः पलायते ।\nतं संभावयेयम् ।\nअर्हसि मे वाम्यौ दातुमिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"He went to Vamadeva's hermitage and said to the sage, \"Revered one, I have struck a deer and it is fleeing; I would like to catch it. You should give me your two horses.\""}},{"n":51,"text":"तमब्रवीदृषिः ।\nददानि ते वाम्यौ ।\nकृतकार्येण भवता ममैव निर्यात्यौ क्षिप्रमिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sage said to him, \"I will give you my horses; but when your task is done, you must return them to me promptly.\""}},{"n":52,"text":"स च तावश्वौ प्रतिगृह्यानुज्ञाप्य चर्षिं प्रायाद्वाम्यसंयुक्तेन रथेन मृगं प्रति ।\nगच्छंश्चाब्रवीत्सूतम् ।\nअश्वरत्नाविमावयोग्यौ ब्राह्मणानाम् ।\nनैतौ प्रतिदेयौ वामदेवायेति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking the two horses and the sage's leave, he went after the deer in a chariot yoked with them. As he went he said to the charioteer, \"These two jewel-horses are fit for kings, not brahmins. They must not be returned to Vamadeva.\""}},{"n":53,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा मृगमवाप्य स्वनगरमेत्याश्वावन्तःपुरेऽस्थापयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Saying so, he caught the deer, returned to his city and kept the two horses in the inner palace."}},{"n":54,"text":"अथर्षिश्चिन्तयामास ।\nतरुणो राजपुत्रः कल्याणं पत्रमासाद्य रमते ।\nन मे प्रतिनिर्यातयति ।\nअहो कष्टमिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the sage thought, \"The young prince has got a fine pair and is enjoying it; he does not give them back to me. Ah, what a pity.\""}},{"n":55,"text":"मनसा निश्चित्य मासि पूर्णे शिष्यमब्रवीत् ।\nगच्छात्रेय ।\nराजानं ब्रूहि ।\nयदि पर्याप्तं निर्यातयोपाध्यायवाम्याविति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having made up his mind, when a month was complete he told his pupil, \"Go, Atreya. Tell the king: if it is enough for you, return the teacher's horses.\""}},{"n":56,"text":"स गत्वैवं तं राजानमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He went and told the king so."}},{"n":57,"text":"तं राजा प्रत्युवाच ।\nराज्ञामेतद्वाहनम् ।\nअनर्हा ब्राह्मणा रत्नानामेवंविधानाम् ।\nकिं च ब्राह्मणानामश्वैः कार्यम् ।\nसाधु प्रतिगम्यतामिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king replied to him, \"This is a conveyance for kings. Brahmins are unfit for such jewels. What do brahmins need horses for? Go back, and well.\""}},{"n":58,"text":"स गत्वैवमुपाध्यायायाचष्ट ॥","meaning":{"en":"He went and told his teacher."}},{"n":59,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वा वचनमप्रियं वामदेवः क्रोधपरीतात्मा स्वयमेव राजानमभिगम्याश्वार्थमभ्यचोदयत् ।\nन चादाद्राजा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing those unpleasant words, Vamadeva, his mind overcome with anger, went to the king himself and pressed him for the horses; but the king did not give them."}},{"text":"वामदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vamadeva said:"}},{"n":60,"text":"प्रयच्छ वाम्यौ मम पार्थिव त्वं\nकृतं हि ते कार्यमन्यैरशक्यम् ।\nमा त्वा वधीद्वरुणो घोरपाशै-\nर्ब्रह्मक्षत्रस्यान्तरे वर्तमानः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Give me the two horses, king, for your task has been done, which others could not do. May Varuna with his terrible nooses not kill you, standing as you do between brahmin and warrior."}},{"text":"राजोवाच","meaning":{"en":"The king said:"}},{"n":61,"text":"अनड्वाहौ सुव्रतौ साधु दान्ता-\nवेतद्विप्राणां वाहनं वामदेव ।\nताभ्यां याहि त्वं यत्र कामो महर्षे\nछन्दांसि वै त्वादृशं संवहन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Well-trained, tame oxen with good habits are the conveyance of brahmins, Vamadeva. Go on those wherever you wish, great sage; the Vedic metres themselves carry one like you."}},{"text":"वामदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vamadeva said:"}},{"n":62,"text":"छन्दांसि वै मादृशं संवहन्ति\nलोकेऽमुष्मिन्पार्थिव यानि सन्ति ।\nअस्मिंस्तु लोके मम यानमेत-\nदस्मद्विधानामपरेषां च राजन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Vedic metres do carry one like me in the other world, king, in all that exist there; but in this world this is my conveyance, and of others like me, king."}},{"text":"राजोवाच","meaning":{"en":"The king said:"}},{"n":63,"text":"चत्वारो वा गर्दभास्त्वां वहन्तु\nश्रेष्ठाश्वतर्यो हरयो वा तुरंगाः ।\nतैस्त्वं याहि क्षत्रियस्यैष वाहो\nमम वाम्यौ न तवैतौ हि विद्धि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let four donkeys carry you, or the best mules, or bay horses; go with them, for this is a warrior's vehicle. Know that the two horses are mine, not yours."}},{"text":"वामदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vamadeva said:"}},{"n":64,"text":"घोरं व्रतं ब्राह्मणस्यैतदाहु-\nरेतद्राजन्यदिहाजीवमानः ।\nअयस्मया घोररूपा महान्तो\nवहन्तु त्वां शितशूलाश्चतुर्धा ॥","meaning":{"en":"They call this the harsh vow of a brahmin, king, that he be not kept alive here without it. May great iron beings of terrible form, with sharp spears, carry you off in four ways."}},{"text":"राजोवाच","meaning":{"en":"The king said:"}},{"n":65,"text":"ये त्वा विदुर्ब्राह्मणं वामदेव\nवाचा हन्तुं मनसा कर्मणा वा ।\nते त्वां सशिष्यमिह पातयन्तु\nमद्वाक्यनुन्नाः शितशूलासिहस्ताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let those who know you as a brahmin, Vamadeva, to kill by word, mind or deed, strike you down here with your pupil, driven by my command, holding sharp spears and swords."}},{"text":"वामदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vamadeva said:"}},{"n":66,"text":"नानुयोगा ब्राह्मणानां भवन्ति\nवाचा राजन्मनसा कर्मणा वा ।\nयस्त्वेवं ब्रह्म तपसान्वेति विद्वां-\nस्तेन श्रेष्ठो भवति हि जीवमानः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins are not called to account, king, by word, mind or deed. The learned man who follows the Veda with austerity becomes the foremost while he lives."}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":67,"text":"एवमुक्ते वामदेवेन राज-\nन्समुत्तस्थू राक्षसा घोररूपाः ।\nतैः शूलहस्तैर्वध्यमानः स राजा\nप्रोवाचेदं वाक्यमुच्चैस्तदानीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Vamadeva had said this, king, fearsome demons rose up. Struck by them with their spears, that king said loudly:"}},{"n":68,"text":"इक्ष्वाकवो यदि ब्रह्मन्दलो वा\nविधेया मे यदि वान्ये विशोऽपि ।\nनोत्स्रक्ष्येऽहं वामदेवस्य वाम्यौ\nनैवंविधा धर्मशीला भवन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If, brahmin, the Ikshvakus, or Dala, or any others of the people are to obey me, I will not give up Vamadeva's horses; such people are not those who keep dharma.\""}},{"n":69,"text":"एवं ब्रुवन्नेव स यातुधानै-\nर्हतो जगामाशु महीं क्षितीशः ।\nततो विदित्वा नृपतिं निपातित-\nमिक्ष्वाकवो वै दलमभ्यषिञ्चन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he said this, the lord of the earth, killed by the demons, quickly fell to the ground. Learning that the king was slain, the Ikshvakus then consecrated Dala as king."}},{"n":70,"text":"राज्ये तदा तत्र गत्वा स विप्रः\nप्रोवाचेदं वचनं वामदेवः ।\nदलं राजानं ब्राह्मणानां हि देय-\nमेवं राजन्सर्वधर्मेषु दृष्टम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that brahmin Vamadeva went there to the new king and said, \"King, it has been seen in all the dharmas that the horses should be given to brahmins.\""}},{"n":71,"text":"बिभेषि चेत्त्वमधर्मान्नरेन्द्र\nप्रयच्छ मे शीघ्रमेवाद्य वाम्यौ ।\nएतच्छ्रुत्वा वामदेवस्य वाक्यं\nस पार्थिवः सूतमुवाच रोषात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If you fear unrighteousness, lord of men, give me the two horses at once today.\" Hearing Vamadeva's words, that king spoke to his charioteer in anger."}},{"n":72,"text":"एकं हि मे सायकं चित्ररूपं\nदिग्धं विषेणाहर संगृहीतम् ।\nयेन विद्धो वामदेवः शयीत\nसंदश्यमानः श्वभिरार्तरूपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Bring me one of my arrows, of varied make and smeared with poison, so that, struck by it, Vamadeva will lie down bitten by dogs and in torment.\""}},{"text":"वामदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vamadeva said:"}},{"n":73,"text":"जानामि पुत्रं दशवर्षं तवाहं\nजातं महिष्यां श्येनजितं नरेन्द्र ।\nतं जहि त्वं मद्वचनात्प्रणुन्न-\nस्तूर्णं प्रियं सायकैर्घोररूपैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I know that you have a ten-year-old son, born of your queen, called Shyenajit, king. Driven by my word, strike him down quickly with the terrible arrows."}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":74,"text":"एवमुक्तो वामदेवेन राज-\nन्नन्तःपुरे राजपुत्रं जघान ।\nस सायकस्तिग्मतेजा विसृष्टः\nश्रुत्वा दलस्तच्च वाक्यं बभाषे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Told so by Vamadeva, king, he killed the prince in the inner palace by the arrow. The sharp-pointed arrow was sent, and Dala, hearing that report, said:"}},{"n":75,"text":"इक्ष्वाकवो हन्त चरामि वः प्रियं\nनिहन्मीमं विप्रमद्य प्रमथ्य ।\nआनीयतामपरस्तिग्मतेजाः\nपश्यध्वं मे वीर्यमद्य क्षितीशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Ikshvakus, I will do something you will like. I will crush this brahmin and kill him today. Bring another sharp-pointed arrow; see my prowess today, kings.\""}},{"text":"वामदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vamadeva said:"}},{"n":76,"text":"यं त्वमेनं सायकं घोररूपं\nविषेण दिग्धं मम संदधासि ।\nन त्वमेनं शरवर्यं विमोक्तुं\nसंधातुं वा शक्ष्यसि मानवेन्द्र ॥","meaning":{"en":"This terrible arrow you fit to your bow, smeared with poison, you will not be able to loose, king, nor to set it."}},{"text":"राजोवाच","meaning":{"en":"The king said:"}},{"n":77,"text":"इक्ष्वाकवः पश्यत मां गृहीतं\nन वै शक्नोम्येष शरं विमोक्तुम् ।\nन चास्य कर्तुं नाशमभ्युत्सहामि\nआयुष्मान्वै जीवतु वामदेवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ikshvakus, see me held fast: I cannot loose the arrow and I cannot bring myself to destroy it. May Vamadeva live long."}},{"text":"वामदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vamadeva said:"}},{"n":78,"text":"संस्पृशैनां महिषीं सायकेन\nततस्तस्मादेनसो मोक्ष्यसे त्वम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Touch this queen with the arrow, and then you will be freed from that sin."}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":79,"text":"ततस्तथा कृतवान्पार्थिवस्तु\nततो मुनिं राजपुत्री बभाषे ।\nयथा युक्तं वामदेवाहमेनं\nदिने दिने संविशन्ती व्यशंसम् ।\nब्राह्मणेभ्यो मृगयन्ती सूनृतानि\nतथा ब्रह्मन्पुण्यलोकं लभेयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king then did so. Then the king's daughter-in-law spoke to the sage: \"Vamadeva, as is fitting, I have been entering the palace daily, begging brahmins for truthful and kind words, so that I may win a world of merit.\""}},{"text":"वामदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vamadeva said:"}},{"n":80,"text":"त्वया त्रातं राजकुलं शुभेक्षणे\nवरं वृणीष्वाप्रतिमं ददानि ते ।\nप्रशाधीमं स्वजनं राजपुत्रि\nइक्ष्वाकुराज्यं सुमहच्चाप्यनिन्द्ये ॥","meaning":{"en":"You, fair-eyed one, have saved the royal house. Choose a matchless boon and I will give it. Rule this kinsfolk, princess, and the great Ikshvaku kingdom, faultless one."}},{"text":"राजपुत्र्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"The princess said:"}},{"n":81,"text":"वरं वृणे भगवन्नेकमेव\nविमुच्यतां किल्बिषादद्य भर्ता ।\nशिवेन चाध्याहि सपुत्रबान्धवं\nवरो वृतो ह्येष मया द्विजाग्र्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"I choose one boon only, revered one: let my husband be freed from sin today. Go with him, with his sons and kin, in peace; this is the boon I have chosen, best of brahmins."}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":82,"text":"श्रुत्वा वचः स मुनी राजपुत्र्या-\nस्तथास्त्विति प्राह कुरुप्रवीर ।\nततः स राजा मुदितो बभूव\nवाम्यौ चास्मै संप्रददौ प्रणम्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the princess's words, the sage said, \"So be it,\" hero of the Kurus. Then the king was delighted, and bowing he gave Vamadeva the two horses."}}]}]}